+# PowerNap v0.2.3-nightcapture — overnight RAW capture
+
+This build is intended to collect a real **awake -> sleep -> sleeping** session before we redesign the sleep-onset detector.
+
+## What is different
+
+`RAW sleep capture` is a dedicated laboratory mode:
+
+- CSV RAW logging is forced ON.
+- The existing detector still runs and writes `SNAP` rows and a `DETECTOR_SLEEP_MARKER` event.
+- A detector `SLEEP_CONFIRMED` result **does not stop sensors**.
+- No 10-minute power-nap alarm is scheduled in this mode.
+- Capture continues until the user presses **STOP / CANCEL**.
+- RAW CSV is rotated at 10 MiB into one logical session:
+  - `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-000.csv`
+  - `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-001.csv`
+  - ...
+- Every 5 minutes an event `CAPTURE_HEARTBEAT` records battery percentage, screen interactive state, and age of the last ACC/HR/IBI callback.
+- The monitoring service uses `START_REDELIVER_INTENT`, so Android can restart it with the same start intent if the service process is reclaimed.
+
+## Tonight's recommended setup
+
+1. Install/build the **samsungDebug** flavor.
+2. On the watch open **Power Nap Lab**.
+3. Select **Samsung Health Sensor SDK** as `READ ENGINE` so the whole recording uses one known sensor path. Avoid `Auto` for this reference recording unless Samsung SDK cannot start.
+4. Enable **RAW sleep capture**. `Record sensor data` is automatically enabled and locked ON.
+5. Make sure sensor/background permissions are granted.
+6. Exact-alarm permission is not required for RAW sleep capture because this mode intentionally schedules no nap alarm.
+7. Wear the watch normally and reasonably snugly. Start with enough battery for the intended capture and avoid enabling battery-saver mode during the experiment if possible.
+8. Press **START** shortly before trying to sleep. From then on, leave the app alone.
+9. If the UI later says `SLEEP_CONFIRMED`, that is only the old detector's marker. **Recording continues.**
+10. After waking, open the app and press **STOP / CANCEL** before pulling files.
+
+## Pull the complete newest session
+
+If one watch is connected:
+
+```bash
+./scripts/pull-sessions.sh \
+  --package com.example.powernapwatch \
+  --latest \
+  --output powernap-night \
+  --timeout 180
+```
+
+If ADB sees more than one device, add the watch serial:
+
+```bash
+./scripts/pull-sessions.sh \
+  --package com.example.powernapwatch \
+  --latest \
+  --output powernap-night \
+  --serial 'YOUR_WATCH_SERIAL' \
+  --timeout 180
+```
+
+`--latest` now detects rotated files and downloads **all segments belonging to the newest session**.
+
+## Quick integrity check
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/analyze-session.py powernap-night
+```
+
+For the final analysis, provide every `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-NNN.csv` file from that session. Do not merge or edit them manually; the global `seq` column preserves ordering across segments.
+
+## Expected size
+
+Previous captures were approximately 7 MiB/hour at the current Samsung RAW rates. A full night may therefore produce tens of MiB. Rotation at 10 MiB keeps each individual file manageable while retaining all samples.
